diff --git a/apt/README.md b/apt/README.md
index 4788651..d3f7162 100644
--- a/apt/README.md
+++ b/apt/README.md
@@ -19,3 +19,37 @@ empty interface libraries keep runtime-only files out of direct `DT_NEEDED`
 entries, while their declared SONAME filenames enter Bazel's solib directories
 and runtime search paths. Plain `data` files and `additional_linker_inputs` do
 not provide that runtime linking interface.
+
+## Shared sources and reviewed locks
+
+Declare the project source document once with
+`apt.sources_file(file = "//apt:sources.json")`. Dependencies may repeat the
+same document. A root `override = True` selects a different baseline for the
+whole graph. Legacy declarations may select a subset of its architectures;
+URI or component conflicts fail before downloading indices.
+
+Use `apt.import_lock(lock = "//apt:apt.lock.json", libraries = True,
+sources = "//apt:sources.json", requests = "//apt:requests.json")` to expose
+payload, control archives, existing package/header/pkgconfig targets, and
+individual `libNAME_cc`, `libNAME_shared`, `libNAME_static` targets when the
+DEB contains those libraries. Each package identity has one shared legacy leaf
+repository. Repeated payload/library views reuse that repository. Library
+imports require the reviewed `packages[key].files` map. Target and execution
+platforms select the toolchain and architecture; imports do not choose a C/C++
+toolchain. Shared-library execution follows the deployment loader search path.
+
+Normal imports never fetch package indices or rewrite the lock. Every
+`apt.install` request in a dependency must appear in the lock's recorded inputs;
+changed sources, requests, or package closure require an explicit lock update.
+The `_inputs` record binds full `source_document`, `requests_document`, and
+`module_requests_document` objects.
+
+For explicit updates, read requests with `apt.install_file(file =
+"//apt:requests.json")`, add root `apt.export_lock(name = "apt_lock_export",
+previous_lock = "//apt:apt.lock.json")`, and build `@apt_lock_export//:lock`.
+The target exports `apt.lock.json` on both Bazel facts and lockfile paths. It
+records `packages[key].files`, actual index integrity in `facts`, and normalized
+MODULE requests in `_module_requests`. The update driver validates existing
+package identities and binds reviewed input documents before replacing the
+production lock. `previous_lock` supplies preferred existing versions and fixed
+index integrity; an incompatible constraint must be reviewed by the driver.
